questions.explanation:
SA 320 explicitly requires the auditor to document the following amounts and the factors considered in their determination:
(a) Materiality for the financial statements as a whole;
(b) If applicable, the materiality level or levels for particular classes of transactions, account balances or disclosures;
(c) Performance materiality; and
(d) Any revision of (a)–(c) as the audit progressed.
Personal tax returns of engagement team members (Item V) are entirely irrelevant to audit documentation under SA 320. Thus, Items I, II, III and IV are required.
